      "status": "pass",
      "source_evidence": "The state space is R^m and the Jacobian acts on component vectors.",
      "translation_evidence": "Coordinate operations are pointwise, matrix action is the ordinary row sum, and differentiation uses the usual finite-dimensional topology.",
      "reasoning": "The component semantics agree. Equivalent finite-dimensional norms do not change the derivative or spectral criterion."
    },
    {
      "id": "N03",
      "status": "not-applicable",
